        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8269b585-8ce5-5fac-b1ef-15abe8c65b6c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Appeal to Reason, The Cooperative Commonwealth\n- People: Julius Wayland, Laurence Gronlund, Karl Marx, Ferdinand Lassalle, Edward Bellamy\n- Organizations: Farmers' Alliance\n- Topics: American socialism, International Socialism, agrarian movements, left-wing political newspapers\n\nFacts:\n- The Farmers' Alliance was an organized agrarian economic movement among American farmers that developed and flourished in 1875.\n- In 1884, Laurence Gronlund published The Cooperative Commonwealth, a popular book that adapted the International Socialism of Karl Marx and Ferdinand Lassalle to an American idiom.\n- Laurence Gronlund influenced the thinking of Edward Bellamy, Julius Wayland, and the American socialist movement of the 1880s and 1890s.\n- Julius Wayland is best known for publishing Appeal to Reason, a socialist publication often regarded as the most important socialist periodical of its time.\n- Appeal to Reason was a weekly left-wing political newspaper published in the American Midwest from 1895 until 1922.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
